Z||000000||1FST2M6||09-24-2001||11:58 AM||||what do you think.. the drums on a Dynojet weigh 3600 pounds; my car doesnt' weigh that much but the added weight should offset the wind drag, and rolling resistance of the front wheels that sound about right? had my car on the dyno this weekend just for $hits and giggles we ran a standing start 0-60 on nitrous... it pulled to 60mph in 4.91 seconds... to nearly 110 just as it slammed into 3rd it back firesd somthing fierce and we quit for the day... <P><B>who wants the MPEG?</B> <P>oh i took RodrV6 for a launch on thursday night...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (as we left the parking lot i nailed it an tossed him into the head rest "i knew you were gunna do that" then on a back road we sat for a second and chatted then i nailed it again "uum it is quite a bit faster than my 88" i; on saturday leaned it out so now it doens't flood and stall when i get off the throttle quick.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ran 9.8-10.2:1 now runs 12.8:1 off idle on the spray. i'm gunna add a 2nd stage to lean it up even more above 3500.. it gets really rich about then. <P>I saw Predators turbo 85 GT down there.. and back it off the dyno.. i LOVE that car...  <P>------------------<BR>12.920@109mph... "thats all I have to say about that"||||reg||1
