Z||000018||Shaun41178||09-24-2001||04:02 PM||||hmm must not like hotmail accounts.  Kind of wish I still had my aol account at a time like this.<P><BR>Just a word about the g-tech.  Yes I actually owned one and yes it did work.  How do I know?  I took mine to the track and compared it to the track times.  My g-tech was less then .1 off the tiems on my printout.  So I think it is pretty accurate.  As far as mph though it was 2-3 mph faster then the printout at the track cause the g-tech and the track measure mph differently.<P>MikeFD3S I don't know if you have ever used one or not but if you have then you would know that they are pretty accurate if hooked up properly.  And when you say "both ways" what do you mean?  It measure more then 2 things.  so by you saying that it almost seems like you have never used one.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com||||reg||1
