Z||000040||OcalaFiero||09-25-2001||09:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B><P>MikeFD3S I don't know if you have ever used one or not but if you have then you would know that they are pretty accurate if hooked up properly.  And when you say "both ways" what do you mean?  It measure more then 2 things.  so by you saying that it almost seems like you have never used one.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>By "both ways" he wansn't referring to your "lifestyle" or anything, He was probably referring to the fact that the G Tech is pretty inaccurate in measuring 1/4 mile and 0-60 times. You may have gotten lucky and had it come out close to your "time sheet", but, G-Tech's are notorious for being inaccurate. This is coming from an engineer that has compared them to all of the other methods of measuring time/speed/distance. In college we did an experiment by taking 3 Gtechs (ramndomly selected) and placed all 3 in the same car, at the same time, ran a quarter mile, and got 3 widely different results. But G Techs do look cool in the mall/high school parking lot I guess. <P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR>'86 2M4<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallsigpic_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
